A helper builds a lamp, switches it off, and returns. What does the program print?
class Lamp {
    boolean on = true;
}

class Main {
    static void light() {
        Lamp l = new Lamp();
        l.on = false;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        light();
        System.out.println("done");
    }
}

Two nodes exist, one reachable from a static field and one only from a local. After the last lines run, what can the collector take?
class Node {
    Node next;
}

class Main {
    static Node head = new Node();

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Node t = new Node();
        t.next = head;
        head = null;
        t = null;
        System.out.println("checked");
    }
}

